@startuml run-lifecycle
' UML sequence diagram: one `run`, from preflight to reap.
' Source of record for docs/diagrams/run-lifecycle.svg. Do not edit the SVG:
' render it with the pinned PlantUML image (docs/adopting.md).
' &#45;&#45; is a literal "--": PlantUML reads --text-- as strikeout.
title run: preflight, per-run network, gateway with the grant, jail, reap

actor "operator" as H
participant "agentjail\nrun" as C
participant "podman" as P
participant "gateway container\nclass, dual-homed" as G
participant "jail container\nuid 10000" as J

H -> C : agentjail run <profile> &#45;&#45; <agent command…>
C -> C : load, validate, run the blockers,\nresolve the class, compute the grant
C -> P : image inspect the gateway tag,\nthen start the container by ID, never by tag
C -> P : prune containers and networks whose owning pid is dead\n(never by profile prefix alone)
C -> P : network create &#45;&#45;internal <profile>-<pid>-<class>\nnetwork create <profile>-<pid>-egress
C -> P : network inspect
note over C
  The same verification function `doctor &#45;&#45;network` calls: internal=true,
  a subnet, IPv4 only. A network that changed under you fails before anything
  starts, and a refusal is not a warning.
end note
C -> P : run -d gateway on both networks\n&#45;&#45;grant <profile egress ∩ class allowlist>\n&#45;&#45;audit-dir <state>/audit/<class>
note right of G
  An empty grant is announced ("this jail has no route out"),
  not refused: the gateway starts and permits nothing.
end note
C -> P : read the gateway's address on the class network,\nand fail the run if it never appears
C -> P : run jail &#45;&#45;network class &#45;&#45;dns <gateway>\n&#45;&#45;dns-search . &#45;&#45;env HTTPS_PROXY/ALL_PROXY=http://<gateway>:3128
J -> G : CONNECT host:port, the jail has no other peer
H -> C : SIGINT, SIGTERM, SIGQUIT
C -> P : forward the signal to podman, then wait
P --> C : exit code, or 128 + signal
C -> P : remove the gateway, then the egress network,\nthen the class network, on every exit path
C --> H : exit with the agent's own code
@enduml
